jewbuntu (0.1.0~m1.25+26.04) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Web Server: phpMyAdmin (http://localhost/phpmyadmin, always local-only),
    an FTP server (your Ubuntu login, locked to ~/Sites, local-only unless
    sharing is on, TLS required while sharing), and your own MySQL login with
    show/copy/reset in the app. Servers set up earlier get a "Finish setup" row.
  * Web Server: fix Apache stopping right after setup on systemd machines
    (a reload with changed Listen lines killed it); setup now restarts.
  * GTK4 apps link to the installed skin instead of copying it, so skin
    updates reach them; copies from earlier versions are converted at login.
  * Requires jewbuntu-skin 0.1.0~git20261112.1 (app windows no longer
    see-through).

